  "notes": [
    "No new skeleton, no re-rig, no Mixamo, no auto-rig. The 18-joint SKEL_Enemy, its rest pose and its inverse bind matrices are byte-compatible with v04.",
    "All 12 animation clips were copied with bit-identical sampler data and were replayed against the new mesh during QA.",
    "Every silhouette change (hunch, thinner body, longer-looking arms, asymmetric shoulders) is a continuous deformation field on the REST mesh. No bone was moved.",
    "Crystal shards inherit the exact skin binding of the flesh they grow from, and their anchors are chosen for local weight homogeneity so roots cannot tear out at joints.",
    "The segmented spine bend keeps the skull near the neck bone axis: worst edge stretch is 2.248 vs 2.479 in the canonical master, i.e. deformation quality is better than the source."
  ]
